    }
   ],
   "html": "<p>To spark conversation around the release of Deliver Me From Nowhere, IHC curated an intimate creator trip to NYC to celebrate special pieces of Bruce Springsteen’s iconic musical history showcased in the film.  </p>\n<p>From a festival screening to a visit to Power Station Studios where “Born in the U.S.A.” came to life, creators were immersed in the glamour, anticipation, and cultural spotlight that defined Bruce’s rise.</p>"
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "STUDIO SESSION",
   "pieces": [
    {
     "type": "text2",
     "left": "<p>We brought creators to the studio where demos from Nebraska evolved into Springsteen’s album, Born in the U.S.A. The studio provided a Four-Track technical explanation, detailing how Nebraska was recorded. Pitchfork Founder, Ryan Schreiber, led a Q&amp;A with Lucy Dacus, Matt Berninger, and Walt Martin. The group discussed Springsteen’s influence on their lives before recording songs onto a four-track. </p>",
     "right": "<p>The session concluded with a surprise preview of three unreleased songs from the film’s soundtrack while our content team captured raw reactions. These moments became some of the highest-performing content in the film’s promotional campaign outside of official trailers.The experience highlighted the power of authentic curation, connecting legacy fans with millennial and Gen Z audiences.</p>"
    },
